{
  "title": "Section name title-casing lowercases the word after a hyphen",
  "description": "normalize_section_name / title_case (ramekin-core/src/ingredient_parser/item/line_classifiers.rs) treats a hyphenated word as one word and lowercases everything after its first letter. \
So the Smitten Kitchen header 'Curry-Lime Yogurt' becomes section 'Curry-lime Yogurt' (see data/pipeline-snapshots/smittenkitchen-com_2006-11-throwing-pancakes-to-the-wind.json). \
Capitalize each hyphen-separated part when the source capitalized it (or simply keep a mixed-case source header as written and only normalize ALL CAPS / all-lowercase ones). \
Expect small data/ diffs from make pipeline in section names.",
